      care: "Iolite measures 7–7.5 on the Mohs scale but has perfect cleavage in one direction and fair toughness. Hard blows, extreme pressure, high heat and sudden temperature changes can break it. Warm soapy water is the recommended cleaning method; avoid ultrasonic and steam cleaners, and consider protective settings for rings.",
      faqs: [{ question: "Why can iolite look like different colours from different angles?", answer: "Iolite has strong pleochroism, so its colour can vary with viewing direction. Cut orientation affects the face-up appearance and the colour visible through the gem." }],
